Size the keymapper overlay from its real allocation, not from is_maximized().

A tiling compositor (Hyprland) sizes and tiles windows without ever putting
them in the maximized state, so `self.is_maximized()` is always False there and
this block never runs. The overlay then keeps whatever size the compositor
handed it -- observed 441x705 over a 2625x1410 Android surface -- so the mapped
widgets land on a fraction of the screen. waydroid-helper#106.

Sizing from the allocation is correct on both kinds of compositor: a tiling one
tiles it to the free space, and a floating one maximises it, and either way the
allocation is the area the overlay actually occupies.

--- a/waydroid_helper/controller/app/window.py
+++ b/waydroid_helper/controller/app/window.py
@@ -482,7 +482,7 @@
         Adw.Window().do_size_allocate(self, width, height, baseline)
         sc = ScreenInfo()
-        if self.is_maximized() and sc.host_width == 0 and sc.host_height == 0:
+        if width > 0 and height > 0 and sc.host_width == 0 and sc.host_height == 0:
             width = self.get_allocated_width()
             height = self.get_allocated_height()
